.task-board/EPIC-260720-21aq1i_declarative-compiled-builds/STORY-260720-3plyvy_curator-go-build-driver/TASK-260720-1zntv0_implement-go-v1-preflight-and-build/progress.md:69:Rework logbook 2026-07-21 — stop-the-line architecture conflict confirmed against Go 1.25 and native macOS APIs. The supported-platform AC requires per-child filesystem and network denial plus resource and process-graph controls on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows, while the normative graph permits only direct Go and GOROOT tool executables. Darwin os/exec has no per-child sandbox hook; sandbox_init confines the current process and sandbox-exec is an extra deprecated launcher. Linux requires child pre-exec namespace, Landlock/seccomp/cgroup setup or a broker; Windows needs a custom suspended-process, Job Object, restricted-token/AppContainer subsystem. Post-start observation is racy and permission/environment checks do not enforce denial. Failing closed outside one host contradicts valid real-build support on current CI. No product code changed. Recommended decision: permit one operator-trusted manager-owned sandbox launcher or broker and revise conformance, or explicitly narrow supported build hosts. Full evidence and tradeoffs: TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-policy-blocker.md.
